# taste-skill Reference

This project uses taste-skill design framework for frontend/UI work.

**GitHub Repository:**
https://github.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill

**SKILL.md (Full Guidelines):**
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Leonxlnx/taste-skill/main/SKILL.md

## What is taste-skill?

taste-skill is NOT an npm package. It's a **design instruction framework** for AI agents.
It prevents generic/AI-generated design patterns by enforcing premium design rules.

### How to use:

1. **When designing UI:** Read the design read rules (Section 0) first
2. **Set the dials:** DESIGN_VARIANCE, MOTION_INTENSITY, VISUAL_DENSITY
3. **Follow pre-flight checks:** 50+ mandatory quality gates before shipping
4. **Key rules:**
   - EM-DASH (—) is COMPLETELY BANNED
   - One design system per project
   - Hero fits viewport (no scroll to find CTA)
   - Max 1 eyebrow per 3 sections
   - WCAG AA contrast minimum

### Main Sections:

- **Section 0:** Brief Inference (read the room before coding)
- **Section 1:** Three Dials configuration
- **Section 2:** Design System Map (when to use official packages)
- **Section 3:** Default Stack (React/Next.js, Tailwind v4, Motion)
- **Section 4:** Design Directives (typography, color, layout)
- **Section 5:** Motion & Interactions (Liquid Glass, Magnetic Physics)
- **Section 6:** Performance & A11y (hardware acceleration, dark mode, CWV)
- **Section 7:** Dial Technical Reference
- **Section 8:** Dark Mode Protocol
- **Section 9:** AI Tells (Forbidden Patterns)
- **Section 10:** Pre-Flight Check (50+ checkboxes)

### For this project:

When you ask to build/redesign UI, refer back to this file or the GitHub repo.
The `.instructions.md` file contains the full copied SKILL.md for quick access.
